  "scope": "The literal96-slot power-of-two machine repeatedly executes the real zero test, actual canonical predecessor and recursive child power call, then allocates the returned low false bit. The base allocates literal one. Exact original powerOfTwoBinary raw output, heap/source preservation and paid terminal execution are proved. The bound64*(value(exponent)+1)*(exponent.length+1) is explicitly polynomial in the numerical exponent, not binary exponent length alone; the output itself has value(exponent)+1 bits. Later grid-derived exponent limits, lambda construction and whole solver composition remain separate. Twelve actual physical cases cover zero, padding, recursion and exponent16.",
